<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  World mission driver — launchd job.

  VERSIONED 2026-09-05. Until now this plist existed ONLY in ~/Library/LaunchAgents and
  was unversioned entirely, so its schedule was unreviewable and no change to it left a
  trace — the same trap the motoko plist recorded and fixed on 2026-08-17. Installed
  plists are COPIES, not symlinks: editing this file changes nothing until it is copied
  to ~/Library/LaunchAgents and the job is reloaded.

  SCHEDULE: KeepAlive + ThrottleInterval, NOT StartInterval (Mark, attended 2026-09-05).
  StartInterval re-arms from the job's EXIT, not its start — world measured a 14390s gap
  against its 14400s interval, so the real period was duration + interval, and 19.0 of
  world's 24 hours were idle. ThrottleInterval is measured from the START, so the period
  becomes max(duration, 14400) rather than duration + 14400. The nominal 4h spacing is
  UNCHANGED; only the wasted slot goes. Projected 4.75 -> 6.0 iterations/day on a mean
  duration of 3785s (n=2 — thin, and the durable slot-verdict log added in the same change
  is what will make it n>2).

  ThrottleInterval is load-bearing: the yield paths (kill switch, overlap guard, memory
  gate) exit in seconds and bare KeepAlive would respawn them in a tight loop.

  PREREQUISITE, already landed: world had NO memory gate and NO boot stagger. Raising a
  loop's rate on a box that took three jetsam events in 48h, while that loop is the one
  mission with no admission control, would trade an idle problem for an OOM problem. Both
  are ported and covered by tools/launchd/test_mission_memgate.sh (PASS=24).

  Contends with v1 (90m), docs (6h) and motoko (13h). Do not re-tighten more than one loop
  at a time: on 2026-09-02 three were tightened together and the fleet stall rate went
  6% -> 33% with NO extra starts. Re-read it the next day.

  Revert: delete KeepAlive + ThrottleInterval, restore <key>StartInterval</key> 14400.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>MISSION_PROFILE</key>
		<string>world</string>
	</dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>dev.ailang.mission-world</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/Users/voightkampff/dev/sunholo-data/ailang-world/tools/launchd/mission-control.sh</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/ailang-mission-world.launchd.log</string>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/tmp/ailang-mission-world.launchd.log</string>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>14400</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
